{
  "$schema": "https://aka.ms/codetour-schema",
  "title": "AI-Enabled Codespace Tour",
  "description": "A guided introduction to the AI tooling available in this codespace — agency, agent aliases, and how to use them for Fluid Framework development.",
  "isPrimary": true,
  "steps": [
    {
      "file": ".devcontainer/GETTING_STARTED.md",
      "line": 1,
      "title": "Welcome",
      "description": "This is your AI-enabled codespace. It comes pre-configured with AI CLI tooling on top of the standard Fluid Framework development environment.\n\nThis tour will walk you through the AI-specific features. For full documentation, see the [AI-enabled Codespace documentation](../docs/content/Development-Environment/AI-enabled-Codespace.md)."
    },
    {
      "file": ".devcontainer/GETTING_STARTED.md",
      "line": 9,
      "title": "Install Agency",
      "description": "Agency is installed automatically the first time you run `start`, `dev`, `copilot`, or `oce`. This requires authentication, so watch for a browser window. If automatic installation fails, run `pnpm install:agency` manually.\n\nAgency manages AI agent sessions and supplies consistent profiles and configuration."
    },
    {
      "file": "scripts/codespace-setup/agent-aliases.sh",
      "line": 26,
      "title": "Fluid Development Launcher",
      "description": "**`dev`** launches Copilot CLI through agency with the Nori profile and the ADO, WorkIQ, and EngHub MCP servers. It is the recommended launcher for Fluid Framework feature work, testing, and debugging."
    },
    {
      "file": "scripts/codespace-setup/agent-aliases.sh",
      "line": 31,
      "title": "Copilot Aliases",
      "description": "These aliases launch GitHub Copilot:\n\n- **`copilot`** — Standard GitHub Copilot\n- **`oce`** — On-Call Engineer workflow (switches to ff-oce agent)"
    },
    {
      "file": "scripts/codespace-setup/agent-aliases.sh",
      "line": 41,
      "title": "Starting Agents",
      "description": "Run `start` for an interactive assistant that selects a launcher based on your task. Use `dev` directly for Fluid Framework development, `copilot` for a general Copilot CLI session, or `oce` for on-call engineer workflows."
    },
    {
      "file": ".devcontainer/devcontainer.json",
      "line": 1,
      "title": "Codespace Configuration",
      "description": "This is the repository's default devcontainer profile. Compared with the nested Standard profile, it provides AI launchers, GitHub CLI (`gh`), SSH access, and the container permissions used by agent sandboxing. It defaults to 32 CPUs / 64 GB RAM rather than Standard's 16 CPUs / 64 GB RAM.\n\n**Tip:** Connect from your local terminal with `gh codespace ssh` while using the Codespace's compute and repository context."
    },
    {
      "file": ".devcontainer/GETTING_STARTED.md",
      "line": 1,
      "title": "Next Steps",
      "description": "You're all set! Run `start` for launcher guidance, or use `dev`, `copilot`, or `oce` directly. Check [DEV.md](../DEV.md) for the full development workflow.\n\nFor more information, see the [AI-enabled Codespace documentation](../docs/content/Development-Environment/AI-enabled-Codespace.md)."
    }
  ]
}
